WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
Start with an arbitrary coefficient row, h zero through h n minus

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:04.360
one.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.780
Encode it as the polynomial h of X, with those entries as

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:09.100
coefficients.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.230
We work with X to the n equal to one.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.080
Multiply by X.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.190
Every exponent increases by one.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.860
The last term reaches X to the n, which becomes one.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.760
So the last coefficient moves to the first position, and every other

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.960
coefficient moves one position to the right.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.520
This is exactly one right cyclic shift.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:34.560
For our running example, h is negative one plus X plus X

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.240
squared plus X cubed.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.780
Multiplying by X gives one minus X plus X squared plus X

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:41.400
cubed.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.220
Its coefficients, one, negative one, one, one, form the second row of

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.040
the original matrix.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.720
We have not rearranged the example.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:53.040
The same reasoning works for any power.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.040
Multiplication by X to the r shifts the row r places right.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.900
The coefficient at X to the j becomes h sub j minus

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.780
r, with its index reduced modulo n.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:09.420
The first row is h, the second is X h, and row

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.480
j is X to the j minus one times h.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.800
After the nth row, one more multiplication returns to h.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:21.960
For a precise indexing formula, number both rows and columns from zero.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.720
Then the entry in row r, column j is h sub j

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.460
minus r modulo n.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.220
In dimension four, row two, column one traces back to coefficient three

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.060
of the original row.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:39.260
This translates the entire circulant structure into multiplication, and prepares us to

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.420
compare dot products of arbitrary rows.
